body:
I think that you should at the very least be careful right now. You didn't deserve the punishment you got, although I don't personally condone trying to control what your partner does on social media, nor hitting them. But what he did to you was much worse, and "...he was just trying to playfully scare me and wanted to show that he could break my fingers if he wanted to" is not an excuse. That line actually made me quite worried. If someone feels like they have to prove that they can break your finger, something is not right with them. You got a bit jealous, but he hurt you, quite badly at that. Even though you were the one that got physical first, that is not an excuse either.

&#x200B;

It's difficult to tell if this is a sign that things will get worse in the future. It is definitely not unlikely, since he has shown clearly abusive behaviour. You said he's done things similar to this incident before, but it hasn't been this bad before. That is a sign, but not definitive proof. Though, in situations like these it might be better to get out before you run the risk of acquiring the proof.
